            <details><summary>Is it lakh or lac?</summary><p>Both spellings are understood, but lakh is the spelling used by the Reserve Bank of India and government departments. Use lakh on cheques, invoices and official forms.</p></details>
            <details><summary>How much is 1 million in lakhs, and 1 billion in crores?</summary><p>1 million = 10 lakh (10,00,000) and 1 billion = 100 crore (1,00,00,00,000). Going the other way, 1 crore = 10 million and 1 lakh crore = 1 trillion.</p></details>
            <details><summary>What is the difference between the Indian and the international number system?</summary><p>The Indian system groups digits as 3, then 2, 2, 2 from the right and uses thousand, lakh and crore (1,00,00,000). The international system groups digits in threes and uses thousand, million and billion (10,000,000). The digits are the same, only the commas and the words change.</p></details>
        </div>
    </article>
    </div>
</main>

{% block scripts %}
<script src="/js/number-words.js"></script>
<script>
    function setText(id, text) {
        document.getElementById(id).textContent = text;
    }

    var unitsTimer = null;

    function convertNumber() {
        var inputEl = document.getElementById('numberInput');
        var r = NumberWords.convert(inputEl.value);
        var err = document.getElementById('inputError');
        var box = document.getElementById('answerBox');
        if (r.empty || r.error) {
            err.textContent = r.error || '';
            err.classList.toggle('hidden', !r.error);
            box.classList.add('opacity-40');
            return;
        }
        err.classList.add('hidden');
        box.classList.remove('opacity-40');

        // The answer people came for goes first: digits when they typed lakh or crore, words when they typed digits.
        var meta = r.digitCount + ' digits, ' + r.zeroCount + ' zeros · ' + r.internationalFormat;
        if (r.hasUnits) {
            setText('answerMain', r.indianGrouped);
            setText('answerSub', r.inWords);
            meta += ' · ' + r.plain;
        } else {
            setText('answerMain', r.inWords);
            setText('answerSub', '₹' + r.indianGrouped);
        }
        setText('answerMeta', meta);

        // Let the fresh answer settle in like ink (CSS skips this for reduced motion)
        box.classList.remove('qt-fresh');
        void box.offsetWidth;
        box.classList.add('qt-fresh');

        setText('indianFormat', r.indianFormat);
        setText('indianGrouped', '₹' + r.indianGrouped);
        setText('internationalFormat', r.internationalFormat);
        setText('internationalGrouped', r.internationalGrouped);
        setText('inWords', r.inWords);
        setText('chequeFormat', r.cheque);
        setText('internationalWords', r.internationalWords);

        // Count how often people use the new lakh and crore input (one event after they stop typing).
        clearTimeout(unitsTimer);
        if (r.hasUnits && typeof trackEvent === 'function') {
            unitsTimer = setTimeout(function () {
                trackEvent('number_words_units', { tool_name: 'Number to Words' });
            }, 1500);
        }
    }

    function setExample(value) {
        document.getElementById('numberInput').value = value;
        convertNumber();
        // On phones the buttons sit below the answer, so bring the answer back into view.
        var box = document.getElementById('answerBox').getBoundingClientRect();
        if (box.top < 0 || box.bottom > window.innerHeight) {
            document.getElementById('answerBox').scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
        }
    }

    function copyToClipboard(elementId, event) {
        trackCalculatorUsage('Number to Words', document.getElementById('numberInput').value);
        var text = document.getElementById(elementId).textContent;
        var button = event.target.closest('button');
        window.qt.copy(text, button);
    }

    // Links such as /number-to-words/?n=1.5%20crore open with that amount filled in.
    window.addEventListener('load', function () {
        var n = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('n');
        if (n) document.getElementById('numberInput').value = n.slice(0, 80);
        convertNumber();
    });
</script>
{% endblock %}
